### Tone: End-of-game award: Contrarian, most often on the other side of the truth from everyone else (too high when
### everyone else was too low, or the reverse). $count: those rounds (≥ 1). Amused, faintly suspicious.

award-contrarian-1 =
    The Contrarian award goes to { $name }: { $count ->
        [one] once
       *[other] { $count } times
    } on the opposite side of everyone else. Brave. Lonely. Brave.
award-contrarian-2 = { $name }, when everyone went high, you went low. When they went low, you went high. Was it a strategy? Be honest.
award-contrarian-3 =
    Contrarian: { $name }. { $count ->
        [one] One round
       *[other] { $count } rounds
    } against the swarm’s grain. The swarm finds you exhausting. I find you useful.
award-contrarian-4 = { $name } disagreed with the entire room and stood by it. Sometimes correctly. That’s the annoying part.
award-contrarian-5 = The award for going your own way goes to { $name }. Usually the other way.
award-contrarian-6 = { $name }, the swarm’s natural opposite. Every hive mind needs one. I didn’t ask for one.
award-contrarian-7 =
    { $name } bet against everyone { $count ->
        [one] once.
       *[other] { $count } times.
    } I admire that in a test subject. From a distance.
award-contrarian-8 = Contrarian: { $name }. If everyone else is wrong in one direction, you are reliably wrong in the other.
award-contrarian-9 = { $name } refuses to follow the swarm. I respect it. I also average it away. Sorry.
award-contrarian-10 = The Contrarian goes to { $name }, who looked at the consensus and thought: no. Statistically refreshing.
